      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not quite correct. If we would have an identity color space conversion based on the dst target space being sRGB (since primitive colors are defined in sRGB by default), but `skipColorXform \u003d false`, then we would use a ColorSpaceXformPremul block with uniform values that cause it to evaluate as if it were an identity function.  If `skipColorXform \u003d true`, then in this case we\u0027d optimize all the way down to `Passthrough` and truly do no extra work (which is what we want in the hard-coded drawShadows case).\n\nThis means that when `skipColorXform \u003d true` (and since we always have an identity CS function), it will never be shareable with another pipeline with `skipColorXform\u003d false`.",
